hey what's up guys it's rob you know  those little helicopter toys that you  can kind of twist in your hand and they  spin and fly down well i decided to try  to make one of those out of paper  i called jeremy shafer to see if he  wanted to design one too and he  definitely wanted to give it a shot we  folded  and tried a whole bunch of different  models for the paper helicopter spinners  well it took a little time to design one  that flew well we wound up creating two  or our very own designs for helicopter  spinners the cool thing about mine is  that not only can you throw it like a  dart like this and play catch with it if  you want but with a little  adjustment of the propellers once you  give it a spin it'll gently float down  to the ground  it's quick easy and a lot of fun for  everyone it's the propeller spinner  for the tutorial i'm going to be using a  white sheet of printer paper but you can  also use  a colored sheet or even origami paper  some of the folding gets a little thick  during certain parts so i wouldn't  recommend using cover or construction  paper  once you have the paper we can get  started  take the upper right corner and fold it  to the left side so that the top edge is  aligned and then you could remove the  excess paper by either tearing it  or cutting it with scissors now your  paper should have  a diagonal fold in it going from the top  left to the bottom right  [Music]  now that we have a diagonal crease going  this way we're going to take the upper  left corner and fold it down to the  bottom right corner  make a sharp crease and when you open it  you'll see an x in the paper  take the top and fold it down to the  bottom and once again align it and make  a nice sharp crease  open it back up twist it 90 degrees and  then fold the opposite edge  onto the bottom and once again crease it  when you open it up you'll see we now  have an  x and a plus in the paper now we can  take the top and bottom edges and fold  it directly onto the horizontal middle  line  crease it well and then do the same for  the bottom edge  once you open it you'll then see four  new horizontal sections in the paper  turn it 90 degrees and do the same with  the other top edge  and the bottom edge by folding them into  the center horizontal line  when we've finish the precreases we'll  have 16 squares in the paper  along with the plus and the x and we can  move on  [Music]  we're now going to turn the paper into a  modified pinwheel base that looks just  like this  to do that we can just re-crease the  paper on the diagonals like that  and then we're going to pinch the  corners  on the bottom here and push inwards  on the left and right edges with our  finger like this  as you can see the flaps are kind of  sticking up just flatten them down  like this and press it down so that the  paper looks like an upside down t  now we could flip it around and do the  same on this side  pinch the corners together so that the  edges come together and press them  inwards flattening out the entire paper  in the process  and it should look like this now we  could flip it over  and just make sure it's nice and flat  take the bottom and fold it to the top  sort of like a hot dog  and press down to ensure it's creased  sharply you'll notice there's two flaps  on the right or points and two on the  left  in between there's a v-shaped fold we're  going to take our finger and  press on that fold so that it rests  against the center of the paper  so we can just flip that fold by  pressing in the center here  and closing the two flaps on it flatten  the right side out  and then we can repeat it on the left  side open the two flaps and press  upwards on the bottom of the v in the  center so that the valley fold gets  tucked into the middle  you may need to press in the middle of  the v here to reverse the fold  and then once again close the two left  flaps  and flatten the paper out by pressing on  it when you've completed all the folds  the model should look just like this  i've drawn a vertical line where you  should see a crease in the middle of  your paper on both sides  you'll also see that there are two  foldable layers on the right and  two on the left take the top edge here  on the right top layer and fold it  directly next to the vertical line  leaving a small amount of space  once it's lined up just crease it on the  new fold and it will look like this  now we could take that new crease on the  right top edge and fold it to the middle  again  so just hold the center in place with  your left hand here  round the outside edge inwards a bit so  we could fold it into the center line as  well  so just round it and line it up with the  center it gets a little thick  but once it's lined up just crease it  all the way down  and make sure it's nice and flat once  you're finished it should look like this  now we're going to take the top left  edge and flip it over to the right  side flatten it out and do the same  exact thing  take the top edge here fold it next to  the center  line leaving a little bit of space once  again take the outside crease edge  round it into the middle and give it a  firm press and crease  trying to flatten it out so it lies on  top of the other one  the front of the paper should look like  this now  now we can flip it over and do the same  thing the top right edge into the middle  and then the outside edge into the  middle take the last  left flap flip it to the right side and  once again  fold the top edge into the middle and  then fold the outside into the middle  and flatten it out really well  now the paper should look like this and  this is the dark configuration and it  should look like an  arrow you can try throwing it like this  but now we can move on  [Music]  now that we have a model that looks like  this you can see i've drawn  a line at the base of the propeller  where you should notice an edge that  wraps around it here  we're going to grab one propeller with  our right thumb and pointer  and the opposite one with our left hand  and press gently in the middle so we  form  a cross or plus at this point  we're going to fold the propeller  downwards away from us  along that line that i've drawn so that  it lies  flat so just pinch it down just like  this  so that it looks something like that  then all we need to do is just  turn it and do the same thing with the  next one fold it back away from you and  give it a pinch at that crease  and finally the last two fold it back  and pinch it turn it  fold it back and pinch it so it looks  like a little ninja star  and we're ready to give it a test throw  okay so at this point i'm just going to  take it here and i'm just going to throw  it and i know it's probably not going to  spin  because we have to adjust it a little  bit but what i'm going to do is just  hold it like this and just  toss it out sort of like a dart  well it actually spun a little bit i'm  going to flatten it  i'm going to take these two edges and  squeeze them together like this  and take these two right edges and  squeeze them together  and just push it here just very gently  and then kind of push in the middle  and then try it again  there you go so now it's spinning a lot  more so you don't want these folded very  hard  but you're going to do that initially at  this little  crease right here fold it down but then  we're going to flatten it out a little  push gently hold it here like this and  just toss it out  it should also automatically spin if you  drop it so let's do the drop test  thanks for watching my tutorial for the  paper helicopter spinner i hope you guys  enjoyed it and that you were able to get  it to spin be sure to adjust it and to  make sure that the propellers are flat  and  facing up slightly like that not folded  too far down otherwise it won't spin  properly if you did enjoy the video be  sure to give it a thumbs up down below  and also be sure to subscribe and click  that notification bell if you haven't  already thank you guys so much for the  comments and support in the last video i  read i think  almost every comment and they were all  awesome so i really appreciate it and i  got some new content headed your way so  be sure to click that notification bell  and i'll see you soon

